{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":27859,"name":"Ebube Chukwuma","username":"ebubedev","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/talk.nervos.org/ebubedev/{size}/10679_2.png","created_at":"2026-11-26T12:40:19.312Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003ePeople kept getting stuck on the same thing (esp. some of my Twine beta tester). They could create an invoice, and then nobody could pay it. No inbound liquidity, no route, and no obvious way to fix either one without finding a peer and opening a channel first.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat is what \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/nervosnetwork/fiber/pull/1766\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eFiber PR #1766\u003c/a\u003e i opened adds to Fiber. A receiver with no channel can still be paid in CKB. The receiver registers with a liquidity node. The invoice names that node. If there is no route, the liquidity node opens a private CKB channel sized for that payment and forwards it once the channel is ready.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe pull request is open. It is not merged, and it is not in an official \u003ccode\u003efnn\u003c/code\u003e release yet. Review is welcome on the PR.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eStudio LSP\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/chukwuma619/studio-lsp\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eStudio LSP\u003c/a\u003e is the liquidity node I created and deployed for this. LSP means liquidity service provider: a Fiber node whose job is to open channels so another node can receive, and to sit on the other side of a channel when that node wants to send.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt is a normal Fiber node with a public address, funded with CKB, and configured as a just-in-time liquidity service. Your node still runs on your machine. Your keys stay with you. Studio LSP is the peer the payment uses.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt is a Fiber service, not a Fiber Studio feature. Any Fiber node that speaks this protocol can use it: \u003ccode\u003efnn\u003c/code\u003e, fiber-wasm, and fiber-js. The repo has the testnet pubkey, the address, and the config to register your own node.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTwo cases:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eReceive, and you have no channel.\u003c/strong\u003e Your node registers with Studio LSP. The invoice points at it. The sender pays Studio LSP, Studio LSP opens a private CKB channel to you, funds it, and forwards the payment. You end up with a channel and the CKB.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSend.\u003c/strong\u003e You open a private CKB channel to Studio LSP with your own funds. Studio LSP accepts and locks 1,000 CKB on its side. That balance is what you can receive later on the same channel.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTrying it today\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOfficial Fiber does not include this yet, so a released \u003ccode\u003efnn\u003c/code\u003e cannot register with Studio LSP. Fiber Studio 1.1.6 is the current way to try it, because that build bundles the JIT branch. Once the pull request is in a Fiber release, the same Studio LSP works from any node. The connection steps are in the \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/chukwuma619/studio-lsp\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003erepo\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn testnet, with \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/chukwuma619/fiber-studio/releases/tag/v1.1.6\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eFiber Studio 1.1.6\u003c/a\u003e (\u003cstrong\u003eSettings → Updates\u003c/strong\u003e, or \u003ca href=\"https://www.getfiberstudio.com/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003egetfiberstudio.com\u003c/a\u003e):\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eStart the node on testnet. It connects to Studio LSP on its own.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCreate a CKB invoice. A channel does not need to exist first.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eHave someone pay it. If you have no inbound route, Studio LSP opens a private channel and the payment lands.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAdd on-chain CKB when you want to send. The channel to Studio LSP is opened for you.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLimits on the testnet node\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCKB only. UDT and Lightning are unchanged. Mainnet is not served by this node yet.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"md-table\"\u003e\n\u003ctable\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003cth\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eTestnet\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eWho pays when a receive has to open a channel\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eThe sender, 10 CKB\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eSmallest payment that can open a channel\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e100 CKB\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eLargest amount above the channel reserve\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e9,900 CKB\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eInbound left after that first payment\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eAbout 900 CKB, so a later receive can use the same channel\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eWhen you open a channel to send\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eStudio LSP locks 1,000 CKB on its side\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp\u003eA receive fails if your node is offline, or if Studio LSP is offline or out of CKB. A second payment waits if the first channel is still opening. It does not reuse funding that was sized for the earlier payment.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you want to try a receive with no channel, use the 1.1.6 build on testnet. If you run Fiber yourself, read the flow in \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/nervosnetwork/fiber/pull/1766\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ePR #1766\u003c/a\u003e and the node setup in \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/chukwuma619/studio-lsp\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003estudio-lsp\u003c/a\u003e. Comments on a receive that should have worked and did not are the most useful.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eConfirm it\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUpdate to Fiber Studio 1.1.6, start on testnet, and create a CKB invoice for \u003cstrong\u003e100 CKB\u003c/strong\u003e. Leave the description empty or put “JIT test”. You do not need a channel open first. Paste the invoice in a reply here.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e100 CKB is the smallest amount this node will open a channel for. I will pay each invoice when I see it. Keep your node running until the payment shows up.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":1,"updated_at":"2026-11-26T12:40:19.312Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":9,"reads":23,"readers_count":22,"score":139.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":11375,"topic_slug":"receive-ckb-on-fiber-without-a-channel-or-inbound-liquidity","display_username":"Ebube Chukwuma","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://github.com/nervosnetwork/fiber/pull/1766","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"feat: fund just-in-time CKB channels for receivers without a route by chukwuma619 · Pull Request #1766 · nervosnetwork/fiber · GitHub","clicks":4},{"url":"https://github.com/chukwuma619/fiber-studio/releases/tag/v1.1.6","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Release Fiber Studio v1.1.6 · chukwuma619/fiber-studio · GitHub","clicks":1},{"url":"https://github.com/chukwuma619/studio-lsp","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"GitHub - chukwuma619/studio-lsp: Fiber liquidity service that opens a private CKB channel and forwards the paymen